<title>DENMARK: EIB raises four-percent bond offer to 800 mln DKK.</title>
<headline>EIB raises four-percent bond offer to 800 mln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank on Thursday raised a 500 million crown, four-percent bond offer originally announced on November 5 to 800 million crowns, a statement distributed by the Copenhagen Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The bond, maturing in 2003, is to be listed on the exchange on December 10.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
